A||N||4||goldfinger||I have a few small problems.. please help.||||1||
Z||000000||goldfinger||12-18-2000||11:39 PM||||Ok first off, my door hangs down a little bit and I need to know how or if I can fix this. What i mean is that it hangs down a little and trim doenst line up perfect. Also I my doorhandle doesn't work from the inside.. Can I fix this easy? Another thing I got a problem with is when i push the button to roll down my drivers side window it takes like 15 seconds before it starts moving, then it does it really slow, on the passenger it reacts right away but it moves slow as well. Any help on all or any of these problems would help me out. Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||12-19-2000||01:23 AM||||The slow moving windows seems to be a trait of wear, mine move slow too. The delay sounds to me like your switch is dirty or corroded inside.<P>Which trim on the door are you talking about? It could be that the bushings in your hinge are worn out. That will cause the door to sag. You can get new bushings and fix that or the Fiero Store is selling remanufactured hinges for like $40, you'd need two. IMHO it's just easier to replace the bushings. A quick way to tell if it's the bushings is to partially open the door and pick up on the back of the door, if you feel a lot of up and down movement then that is a good sign you need new ones.<P>As far as the inside door handle, you'll have to take it apart and look at it to find out what's wrong with it.<P>Good Luck<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||goldfinger||12-19-2000||02:11 AM||||Thanks, im gonna try to get it all fixed up during christmas break, I will have time and money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Life will be good once im driving my fiero again!! Thanks for the reply!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||12-19-2000||02:21 AM||||When your inside the door looking at the linkage for the handle, Clean out the window tracks and re-grease them. (where the rollers run) This will help the window act like new again. Dirt builds up and slows it down.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-19-2000||09:48 AM||||There are door articles in my cave that should help.<P>The window switches are built such that they collect large amounts of crud. Check these out before messing inside the doors. While they can be taken apart for service, it's easier for most people to get new ones.<P>the interior door handle has dropped the linkage or broken. You'll have to pull the interior panel to work on it.<P>Since you'll need to get in the door to fix the handle, clean and grease all the window track you can get to. Use a light grease like white lithium.||||reg||1
